Let BoringSSL's util/pregenerate (which writes gen/: the perlasm assembly, err_data.cc
and the source lists) run in the release tarball, offline:

- The tarball leaves out test data (e.g. third_party/wycheproof_testvectors/), so some
  globs in build.json match nothing; allow that (the lists they feed are only for tests).
- Drop github.com/hexops/gotextdiff, which is only used to print a diff in -check mode
  and isn't in the tarball; -check still reports out-of-date files.

--- a/third_party/boringssl/src/util/pregenerate/build.go
+++ b/third_party/boringssl/src/util/pregenerate/build.go
@@ -176,9 +176,8 @@
